The fidelity-2 field against FAST: the space-downlink SMF gap (backlog 2-W1, 2-AO)
elevations    : [20.0, 30.0, 60.0, 90.0] deg
trials/field  : 400      samples/FAST: 1000      seed: 20260905      field workers: 16 (process pool)
scenario      : downlink, 1550 nm, 500 km, 700 mm ground SMF, 100 mm space terminal, Cn2_0=1.7e-14
correction    : NONE on every model. Fidelity 2 applies no tip-tilt and no AO (backlog 2-AO), so the FAST NOAO run is the like-for-like pair.
outer scale   : L0 = 25 m on the field AND FAST (a finite L0 makes the SMF loss grid-independent; backlog 2-P5). The analytic term is L0-agnostic.
parity        : same Cn2 (site HV), same outer scale on field and FAST, mean-of-dB on FAST and the field, SMF defocus_m=0 (far field).
mode          : RUN
WARNING: under 1000 trials, so the p1 tail is UNDER-SAMPLED. Read the mean and p5 rows only.

