THE VERDICT
  The gap runs from -0.34 to +0.12 dB across 20 to 90 deg.
  The field does NOT read consistently less loss than FAST. The 2-W1 direction is NOT reproduced here.
  The gap rises from -0.34 dB at 20 deg to +0.12 dB at 90 deg (low elevation = more turbulence).
  0 of 4 elevations sit inside the 2-W1 claim band 0.7 to 2.9 dB.
  DEFOCUS is about zero for the 500 km downlink (far field), so the residual gap is NOT a defocus effect. It is the Airy-versus-Gaussian spot shape of the field against the FAST mode overlap. That is an owner interpretation question. This study does NOT resolve it.
  CAVEAT: this certifies the UNCORRECTED rung only (backlog 2-AO). Fidelity 2 applies no correction, so this is NOT a reference for an AO-corrected link.

